message: "If you use this software, please cite it with the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Agent Quality Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Command-line tools for Linux that put AI coding agents under the quality controls of medicine
  manufacturing (GMP), so that developers and quality managers can check what an agent did instead of
  taking its word for it: a quarantine for suspicious input that a person releases, signatures bound to the
  exact content they approve, change control in which a tool runs the tests and keeps receipts, an audit
  trail written by a separate program, a read-only advisor agent, the qualification of injection detectors
  and AI reviewers, deviation and CAPA handling, and an optional checkpoint that records the agent's
  outbound traffic. Version 0.2 is a preview.
